    "body": "## Summary\n- add a lifecycle-aware attachment panel to job details\n- let the requester upload JPG/PNG/WebP/PDF files up to 10 MiB with plain-language `JOB_VIEWERS`, `PARTICIPANTS` and `EXECUTION_SECRET` choices\n- list only attachment metadata returned by the server-authorized endpoint; non-creators never receive or infer hidden attachment counts\n- allow regular downloads without inline rendering and deliberately disable inline preview for execution secrets\n- download authorized content through a short-lived Blob URL and revoke it after the browser download action\n- show delete controls only where the existing backend lifecycle permits them\n- reload attachment visibility when assignment/status changes so worker execution-secret access disappears immediately after leaving `IN_PROGRESS`\n- teach the shared API client to preserve browser multipart boundaries for `FormData` and support binary Blob responses\n- correct attachment schema documentation to Flyway V37 after tracking destination arrival occupied V36\n\n## Privacy and security\nThe frontend does not implement its own authorization model. It consumes only the filtered metadata/download endpoints; exact location, wallet/payment data, moderation data and storage/encryption internals remain separate. `EXECUTION_SECRET` is never rendered inline and the UI explicitly warns against payment cards, passwords, identity documents and banking credentials.\n\nThe owner sees the configured 12-file limit because the owner sees every attachment. Other users see only the number of attachments currently returned to them, avoiding side-channel disclosure that hidden files exist.\n\n## Validation\nRun production dependency audit, ESLint, Vite build, backend Maven verify, payments smoke, web-container smoke and full runtime smoke. Do not merge unless the latest head is fully green.",
